      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Jayal et al.",
        "AbstractText": "Pseudomonas aeruginosa ATCC 9027 was isolated in 1943 from a case of otitis externa and is commonly employed as a quality control strain for sterility, assessment of antibiofilm agents, and in vitro study of wound infection. Here, we present the 6.34-Mb draft genome sequence and highlight some pertinent genes that are associated with virulence."
      },
